From b2615f68e6ed7219985c3e2b1eeac6c6fa586860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:03:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(resources): convert native vanilla block visuals

Use the accepted native redstone torch textures with plain torch geometry. Java 26.3 adds bulb planes absent from the target Bedrock 1.26.51.1 torch. Keep accepted-pack precedence and export complete block and item models.

Targeted conversion tests cover source precedence and generated models.

Render all sixteen bed items from the target 1.26.51.1 native bed atlas. Preserve Bedrock auxiliary-value order, selected server icon and texture overrides, mapped Java item metadata and later attachable overrides. Replace the Java special-bed item definition with a generated sprite model while retaining placed block behavior.

Render all seventeen glass-pane inventory icons as angled generated plates. The native 1.26.51.1 client shows a flat held pane and an angled inventory plate; its measured front edge and cell size support a GUI rotation of 30/225/0 and scale of 0.75. Read the native terrain atlas in auxiliary-value order, preserve explicit server item icons and atlas overrides, and leave held and placed panes unchanged.
